  "section": "praeparatio",
  "variant": "missae",
  "sung": false,
  "status": "working-edition",
  "notes": "Psalm 42 as the Ordo prints it — verses 1-5, then the Glória Patri, then the antiphon repeated — said alternately by celebrant and ministers at the foot of the altar. It is a document of its own because the rubric omits exactly this much and no more (rubric s01): in Requiem Masses, and in Masses of the season from Passion Sunday through Maundy Thursday inclusive, the psalm, the doxology and the repeated antiphon fall away together while the sign of the cross, the antiphon's first statement and the Adiutórium stay. The transcribed rubric closes a Dominica Passionis usque ad Sabbatum sanctum exclusive — the pre-reform formula — where the 1962 books read usque ad feriam V in Cena Domini inclusive; in the 1962 rite the two mark out the same days, since the reformed Triduum liturgies have no prayers at the foot, and the do header notes it. The psalm text is the Gallican psalter's, translated from the Greek rather than from the Hebrew, which is why w042 is neuter (see its note). Two parses claim less or more than a form alone can carry, and both are editorial: TRISTIS at w030 carries no gender — the two-termination adjective does not mark it and the speaker is whoever says the psalm — while the same word at w074 is feminine because it stands with ánima. meus at w072 is the nominative form: the masculine possessive has no vocative but mi, which the psalter does not use here, so the address is carried by the note (the ruling the corpus made for Agnus). Latin's vocative of meus is mi: the phrase is address, the possessive follows its noun, and the nominative tag stands accepted, both analyzers confirming the form. The doxology here is the missal's setting of the same formula the corpus carries at orationes.gloria-patri, which the Hours punctuate differently (et semper, for et semper:); the two are separate witnesses of one text and are not collated against each other.",
  "source": {
    "method": "Verified by collation against the independent witnesses below: zero substantive divergence once the hand missal's manifest typographical slip at w105 is set aside (declared in the apparatus and in the witness corrigendum header). Accidental variants (punctuation) adjudicated in the apparatus.",
    "witnesses": "witnesses/ordinarium.iudica-me/",
    "apparatus": "witnesses/ordinarium.iudica-me/apparatus.json"
  },
  "analysis_defaults": { "confidence": "high", "sources": ["editorial"], "review": "pending" },
  "analysis_defaults_words": { "confidence": "high", "sources": ["editorial", "whitakers", "collatinus"], "review": "accepted" },
